<section class="pkg-faq-band">
  <div class="container">
    <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    <div class="pkg-faq">
      <details><summary>What is a senior move manager?</summary><p>A senior move manager, sometimes called a later-life move manager, plans and coordinates a move for an older person: sorting and decluttering, packing, the removal, liaison with the estate agent and solicitor, and settling into the new home.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Is a senior move manager the same as a removals company?</summary><p>No. A removals company transports your belongings. A senior move manager also handles the planning, sorting, paperwork coordination and settling in around the removal.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Do I need a senior move manager?</summary><p>You may find one useful if you are downsizing a long-held family home, moving without nearby family, or arranging a parent's move from a distance. For a simple move with plenty of help, a standard removals firm may be enough.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Is the term regulated in the UK?</summary><p>It is not a protected job title, so check what a provider actually does, whether the removal is insured in writing, and whether the quote is fixed before you book.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Does Chayce Properties act as a senior move manager?</summary><p>Yes. Every client has one dedicated coordinator who manages the move from first call to settling in. Chayce is not an estate agent and does not give financial, legal or care advice.</p></details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

